// S-D1 - a PINNING row. Chip-shared memory has static storage, and today that is
// inherited rather than enforced: `extern var` is a module item, so a function body
// cannot parse one at all. Pinned so the notation cannot later widen what it
// inherited without someone deciding to.
fn main() {
    extern var BUF: [u8; 16] chip writes;
    println(0);
}
